# SourceScore — environment variable example
# Copy to .env.local for dev or set in Cloudflare Pages env for production.

# Plausible (privacy-first analytics) — set to enable, leave unset to skip.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=sourcescore.org

# Cloudflare Web Analytics — set the beacon token to enable.
# Get token from: dash.cloudflare.com → Web Analytics → Your site → Snippet
NEXT_PUBLIC_CF_WEB_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=

# Microsoft Clarity — heatmaps + session recordings (free, GDPR-friendly).
# Project created 2026-05-01. ID: wk6sqdp5vn (Wetenschap category, cookies
# disabled for fingerprinting-free / no-consent-banner mode).
#
# Operator setup (one-time):
#   1. Cloudflare Pages → Settings → Environment variables
#   2. Add to BOTH Production and Preview:
#        Variable: NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID
#        Value:    wk6sqdp5vn
#   3. Redeploy. Verify with:
#        curl -sL https://sourcescore.org | grep -o 'clarity.ms/tag/[a-z0-9]*'
#      Expected: clarity.ms/tag/wk6sqdp5vn
#
# Optional operator hardening (Clarity dashboard → Settings):
#   - IP-blokkering: add operator's home/office IP to exclude own browsing
#     from session recordings (reduces noise). Get IP from icanhazip.com.
#   - Funnels: define after Week-1 data lands. Suggested AAERA funnels:
#       Activation: landing → hero_subtool_click event → source-detail page
#       Engagement: landing → 3+ pages
#   - Smart events: import existing Plausible events (hero_subtool_click,
#     top5_click) so they appear in Clarity timeline alongside heatmaps.
#
# What the code already does (auto, no operator action):
#   - components/Clarity.tsx          — script loader, env-gated
#   - components/ClarityRouteTagger   — fires clarity.set('archetype', X)
#                                        on every route change. Filter
#                                        Clarity heatmaps by archetype.
#   - components/ClarityClickListener — fires clarity('upgrade', reason)
#                                        on any element with
#                                        data-clarity-upgrade attribute.
#                                        Hero subtool cards + top-5 CTAs
#                                        are flagged.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=

# IndexNow — for postdeploy ping to Bing + Yandex + Seznam.
# A key has been generated and stored at:
#   public/<key>.txt   (the public verification file; required for trust)
#   .indexnow-key.txt  (local snapshot; gitignored)
# To activate `npm run deploy` IndexNow pings, copy the key from
# .indexnow-key.txt or just `cat public/*.txt` and set this:
INDEXNOW_KEY=

# Google Search Console (URL-prefix property verification)
# At https://search.google.com/search-console → Add property → URL prefix
# → enter https://sourcescore.org → choose "HTML tag" verification → copy the
# content="..." value into the variable below, redeploy, then click "Verify".
# Once verified, you can leave this set or remove it (verification persists).
NEXT_PUBLIC_GSC_VERIFICATION=
